# K816's own linked bytes, compared by tests/compat.rs.
#
# 248 bytes of filler after `align 256`, then the eight guarded bytes: the run
# is $20F8..$20FF and ends on the last byte of the page.  `01..08` in the last
# row is the run; `AD 00 20 60` past the boundary is `main`.
#
# The link is the real test.  ld65 evaluates the `.assert` this section
# carries, and it passes here at the tightest position that still fits.  Add
# one byte of filler and it fails, measured (`postmortem.md` §G.9.2).

